   "id": "q34",
   "number": "34",
   "type": "mcq_single",
   "stem": "Mr Verma and his family are planning to go to their hometown. He has ₹ 15000 with him on his way. Using the clues given below, find the amount left with him when he reaches his hometown.\n\n**Clues:**\n\n(a) He fills up petrol of ₹ 2500 in his car.\n\n(b) He and his family had a lunch of ₹ 4238 at a restaurant.\n\n(c) Then his children took a camel ride for which he paid ₹ 158.\n\n(d) He took sweets of ₹ 1426 from a sweet shop.\n\n(e) He gave ₹ 100 each to five children after he reached his hometown.",
   "options": [
    {
     "label": "A",
     "text": "₹ 6578"
    },
    {
     "label": "B",
     "text": "₹ 6470"
    },
    {
     "label": "C",
     "text": "₹ 8422"
    },
    {
     "label": "D",
     "text": "₹ 6178"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "D",
   "solution": "Amount that Mr Verma has = ₹ 15000\n\nTotal amount he spend\n\n= ₹ 2500 + ₹ 4238 + ₹ 158 + ₹ 1426 + 5 × ₹ 100 = ₹ 2500 + ₹ 4238 + ₹ 158 + ₹ 1426 + ₹ 500 = ₹ 8822 So, amount left with him = ₹ 15000 – ₹ 8822 = ₹ 6178",
   "topics": [
    "Achievers Section"
   ],
   "fields": {
    "Exam": "SOF IMO",
